  "content": "[#bugbounty](target) \n## Scope & Targets\n- **Production Domains:**\n  - https://www.anytask.com/\n  - https://api.anytask.com/\n  - Mobile apps (Android & iOS)\n- **Staging Environment:**\n  - https://anytask.thesecurityteam.rocks/\n  - https://api.anytask.thesecurityteam.rocks/\n\n## Program Rules & Guidelines\n\n### Authorized Testing\n- Test **only in-scope assets** listed above.\n- Use **your own test accounts**—do NOT access or manipulate other users' data.\n- **No direct contact with sellers** on production.\n- Use **staging environment** for testing messaging, quotes, and high-impact vulnerabilities.\n\n### Prohibited Actions\n- No DoS or disruptive attacks.\n- No deletion, modification, or removal of site content belonging to others.\n- No social engineering, phishing, or physical attacks.\n- No testing on out-of-scope subdomains.\n\n### Reporting\n- Use a **kamalesh2428k@bugcrowdninja.com**  pass : **K@malesH** email for test account sign-up.\n- Report only security-relevant issues with proof of concept.\n- Excluded:\n  - P5 or very low-impact issues (e.g., UI/UX quirks without security impact, rate limiting issues, password complexity complaints).\n  - Vulnerabilities needing MITM or physical access.\n  - Deprecated third-party libraries without exploitability.\n  - Any vulnerability without demonstrating an actual attack vector.\n\n### N-Day / Third Party 0-Day Policy\n- Publicly disclosed N-day bugs become in-scope **14 days after public disclosure**.\n\n### Staging Environment Details\n- Use for safe, high-impact testing:\n  - Messaging/Quote functionality\n  - Multi-user affecting bugs\n- Shared admin credentials (for staging task approval):\n  - Username: hacker-anytasks-admin@thesecurityteam.rocks\n  - Password: hacker-anytasks-admin@thesecurityteam.rocks\n- Use test card number for staging payments: `4111 1111 1111 1111`\n- Email access on staging: `http://stagemail.thesecurityteam.rocks/stagemailanytasks.php`\n\n### Important Notes\n- Billing address currently enforced on buyer-side UI only (not API).\n- Avoid noisy or destructive scanning on production.\n- Safe Harbor:  \n  - Research is authorized under CFAA, DMCA exemptions apply.  \n  - Act in good faith, comply with laws and program rules.\n\n## Key Testing Focus Areas\n- Payment & payout logic\n- Account creation, session, and authentication flows\n- File uploads & input validations (XSS, injection)\n- API endpoints for IDOR, SSRF, sensitive data exposure\n- Mobile app APIs and potential token/secret leaks\n\n---\n\n\n",
