  "content": "[[anytask]]\n\n1. **Authentication**\n    \n    - JWT used in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` headers.\n        \n    - Not stored in memory, localStorage, sessionStorage, or visible cookies → likely **HttpOnly cookie or in-memory use**.\n        \n2. **Frontend**\n    \n    - Multiple JS bundles loaded (`dom.js`, `analysis.js`, `vendor.js`) → may contain hidden API endpoints or logic.\n        \n    - Network tab is main place to observe API calls.\n        \n3. **APIs**\n    \n    - `/shopping/basket/apply-discount-code` → requires JWT; could test for **parameter tampering/IDOR**.\n        \n    - `/frontendevents/dl` → event logging endpoint; limited access (400/405 when fuzzed).\n        \n4. **Memory / Storage**\n    \n    - Nothing sensitive found in **Memory snapshot** or **Application storage**.\n        \n    - JS runtime internals like `parseInt`, `onmessage` are normal, not sensitive.\n        \n5. **Security Posture**\n    \n    - Tokens handled securely (not exposed to JS).\n        \n    - Attack surface: mainly API endpoints and frontend JS logic.",
